window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-093.json",{"day":93,"title":"Reconnecting a Divided District","targetWords":[{"word":"throughout","gloss":"遍及","context":"Throughout the last century, a railway station had stood at the edge of a growing district.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"station","gloss":"车站","context":"Throughout the last century, a railway station had stood at the edge of a growing district.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"front","gloss":"正面","context":"The station's front faced the urban center, while its rear opened onto a narrow lane leading to farmland.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"urban","gloss":"城市的","context":"The station's front faced the urban center, while its rear opened onto a narrow lane leading to farmland.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"forward","gloss":"向前","context":"Before moving forward, the team invited residents to describe their routes.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"north","gloss":"北","context":"Looking at a map, they chose a spot north of the old station, where the rail lines curved west.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"inside","gloss":"在里面","context":"Students noted that a block of offices looked welcoming from outside but had no public passage inside.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"west","gloss":"西","context":"Looking at a map, they chose a spot north of the old station, where the rail lines curved west.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"distance","gloss":"距离","context":"The problem was not simply distance.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"spot","gloss":"地点","context":"Looking at a map, they chose a spot north of the old station, where the rail lines curved west.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"ahead","gloss":"在…前面","context":"Ahead lay questions about maintenance, lighting, and cost, but the district had gained something difficult to express in a construction budget: the confidence that its different parts belonged together, rather than remaining isolated fragments of the same town.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"circle","gloss":"圈","context":"The new barrier divided social life: children stopped visiting friends, older residents shopped elsewhere, and a small community gradually lost its place in the town's inner circle.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"block","gloss":"楼宇","context":"Students noted that a block of offices looked welcoming from outside but had no public passage inside.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"district","gloss":"地区","context":"Throughout the last century, a railway station had stood at the edge of a growing district.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"apart","gloss":"分开","context":"As traffic increased, a highway cut across the district and left one village apart from its neighbors.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"overseas","gloss":"在海外","context":"The designers studied examples overseas, including one neighborhood reached via an elevated walkway.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"path","gloss":"小道","context":"Underneath it, a path would continue east toward the market.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"highway","gloss":"公路","context":"As traffic increased, a highway cut across the district and left one village apart from its neighbors.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"elsewhere","gloss":"在别处","context":"The new barrier divided social life: children stopped visiting friends, older residents shopped elsewhere, and a small community gradually lost its place in the town's inner circle.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"aside","gloss":"放到一边","context":"They set fashionable details aside and focused on accessibility.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"border","gloss":"边界","context":"A route could appear open on a map and still be unusable if a locked gate, a steep stairway, or an unclear ownership border stood in the way.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"edge","gloss":"边","context":"Throughout the last century, a railway station had stood at the edge of a growing district.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"east","gloss":"东","context":"Underneath it, a path would continue east toward the market.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"everywhere","gloss":"到处","context":"When the crossing opened, improvements appeared everywhere in small ways.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"bottom","gloss":"底部","context":"A ramp began near the bottom of the bridge, with resting points along its length.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"internal","gloss":"内部的","context":"These internal arrangements mattered as much as external roads.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"bridge","gloss":"桥","context":"A group of planners proposed a bridge linking the rural settlement with a nearby suburb.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"rural","gloss":"乡村的","context":"A group of planners proposed a bridge linking the rural settlement with a nearby suburb.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"zone","gloss":"区域","context":"A delivery driver marked the boundary of an industrial zone where access was restricted.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"barrier","gloss":"障碍","context":"The new barrier divided social life: children stopped visiting friends, older residents shopped elsewhere, and a small community gradually lost its place in the town's inner circle.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"beneath","gloss":"在…之下","context":"Beneath the structure, the ground remained open for community activities.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"village","gloss":"村","context":"As traffic increased, a highway cut across the district and left one village apart from its neighbors.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"onto","gloss":"通向","context":"The station's front faced the urban center, while its rear opened onto a narrow lane leading to farmland.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"anywhere","gloss":"在任何地方","context":"Residents could go anywhere within the connected neighborhood more easily, although inequalities did not disappear overnight.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"inner","gloss":"内部的","context":"The new barrier divided social life: children stopped visiting friends, older residents shopped elsewhere, and a small community gradually lost its place in the town's inner circle.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"nearby","gloss":"附近的","context":"A group of planners proposed a bridge linking the rural settlement with a nearby suburb.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"square","gloss":"广场","context":"The bridge would span the tracks and reach an upper platform beside a public square.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"external","gloss":"外部的","context":"These internal arrangements mattered as much as external roads.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"via","gloss":"经过","context":"The designers studied examples overseas, including one neighborhood reached via an elevated walkway.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"rail","gloss":"铁路","context":"Looking at a map, they chose a spot north of the old station, where the rail lines curved west.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"span","gloss":"跨越","context":"The bridge would span the tracks and reach an upper platform beside a public square.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"lane","gloss":"小路","context":"The station's front faced the urban center, while its rear opened onto a narrow lane leading to farmland.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"map","gloss":"地图","context":"Looking at a map, they chose a spot north of the old station, where the rail lines curved west.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"upper","gloss":"较高的","context":"The bridge would span the tracks and reach an upper platform beside a public square.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"platform","gloss":"平台","context":"The bridge would span the tracks and reach an upper platform beside a public square.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"forth","gloss":"向前","context":"Its purpose was to connect ordinary destinations, so that residents could move back and forth without depending on a car or taking risks at an unofficial crossing.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"suburb","gloss":"市郊","context":"A group of planners proposed a bridge linking the rural settlement with a nearby suburb.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"boundary","gloss":"界限","context":"A delivery driver marked the boundary of an industrial zone where access was restricted.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"corner","gloss":"角落","context":"An older woman drew a circle around a dangerous corner and explained that the lighting there failed every winter.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"somewhere","gloss":"在某处","context":"Clear signs showed visitors how to reach the station entrance rather than leaving them to search somewhere beyond the car park.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"Throughout the last century, a railway station had stood at the edge of a growing district. The station's front faced the urban center, while its rear opened onto a narrow lane leading to farmland. As traffic increased, a highway cut across the district and left one village apart from its neighbors. A journey that had once taken ten minutes now required a long detour. The problem was not simply distance. The new barrier divided social life: children stopped visiting friends, older residents shopped elsewhere, and a small community gradually lost its place in the town's inner circle.","zh":"上个世纪，一座火车站一直位于不断扩大的地区边缘。车站正面朝向城市中心，背面通往一条连接农田的窄巷。随着交通增加，一条公路穿过这里，把一个村庄同邻近社区分隔开。过去十分钟的路程，现在需要绕行很远。问题不只是距离。新的障碍也割裂了社会生活：孩子不再探访朋友，老人去其他地方购物，小社区逐渐失去在城镇核心生活圈中的位置。"},{"en":"A group of planners proposed a bridge linking the rural settlement with a nearby suburb. Looking at a map, they chose a spot north of the old station, where the rail lines curved west. The bridge would span the tracks and reach an upper platform beside a public square. Underneath it, a path would continue east toward the market. This was not meant to be a spectacular landmark. Its purpose was to connect ordinary destinations, so that residents could move back and forth without depending on a car or taking risks at an unofficial crossing.","zh":"规划人员建议建桥，把农村聚落同附近郊区连接起来。他们查看地图后，选中旧车站以北、铁轨向西弯曲的位置。桥将跨越轨道，到达公共广场旁的高处平台。桥下的小路继续向东通往市场。它并不打算成为壮观的地标，而是连接普通目的地，让居民可以来回出行，不必依靠汽车，也不必冒险通过非正式道口。"},{"en":"Before moving forward, the team invited residents to describe their routes. An older woman drew a circle around a dangerous corner and explained that the lighting there failed every winter. A delivery driver marked the boundary of an industrial zone where access was restricted. Students noted that a block of offices looked welcoming from outside but had no public passage inside. These internal arrangements mattered as much as external roads. A route could appear open on a map and still be unusable if a locked gate, a steep stairway, or an unclear ownership border stood in the way.","zh":"在继续推进之前，团队邀请居民描述出行路线。一位老妇人在危险拐角处画了圈，解释那里的照明每到冬天都会失灵。送货司机标出了限制进入的工业区边界。学生发现一栋办公楼外表友好，内部却没有公共通道。这些内部布局与外部道路同样重要。一条路线在地图上看似畅通，但若有上锁的大门、陡峭楼梯或产权边界不明，仍然可能无法使用。"},{"en":"The designers studied examples overseas, including one neighborhood reached via an elevated walkway. They set fashionable details aside and focused on accessibility. A ramp began near the bottom of the bridge, with resting points along its length. Clear signs showed visitors how to reach the station entrance rather than leaving them to search somewhere beyond the car park. Beneath the structure, the ground remained open for community activities. A viewing area offered a broad view, but it was unnecessary to reach the highest level to use the crossing. A useful design should not make physical confidence a condition of participation.","zh":"设计者参考海外案例，其中一个社区通过高架步道连接。他们暂且放下流行装饰，专注于无障碍使用。坡道从桥的低处开始，沿途设有休息点。清楚的标牌指引访客前往车站入口，避免他们在停车场后面四处寻找。桥下地面保持开放，用于社区活动。观景区视野开阔，但使用通道并不需要攀到最高处。实用设计不应把体力和胆量当作参与公共生活的条件。"},{"en":"When the crossing opened, improvements appeared everywhere in small ways. A child could visit a cousin without an adult driving; a shop received customers from the other side. Residents could go anywhere within the connected neighborhood more easily, although inequalities did not disappear overnight. The project showed that infrastructure succeeds when it fits the trips people already want to make. Ahead lay questions about maintenance, lighting, and cost, but the district had gained something difficult to express in a construction budget: the confidence that its different parts belonged together, rather than remaining isolated fragments of the same town.","zh":"通道开放后，细小的改善随处可见。孩子无需大人开车就能探访表亲；商店也迎来另一侧的顾客。居民在相连社区内部各处出行更方便了，尽管不平等并未一夜消失。项目说明，基础设施应当适应人们本来就想进行的出行。接下来仍需处理维护、照明和成本问题，但这一地区获得了难以用建设预算表达的东西：相信各个部分彼此相连，而不是同一座城镇里互相孤立的碎片。"}],"previous":92,"next":94});
